      "value": "@{62df7cd83e007e467295c4e1|full_name}: if you're not worried about implementing HTTPS access control on a server, it generally won't be an issue.\n\nAgain:\n\nReproducing is as simple as starting an HTTPS server (must be HTTPS, not HTTP) with a valid certificate that yt-dlp/AVPro can connect to it, and trying to load a video from that server that doesn't exist (e.g. it 404's) in an AVPro video player in any world.\n\nAlternatively, you could probably point a video player to something like https://vrchat.com/notavideo, and watch the logs for the expected, desired yt-dlp+AVPro errors.\n\nOld (desired) behavior: yt-dlp will see the 404 from the HTTPS link, then VRChat will attempt to load the video in AVPro such that it directly connects. VRC/AVPro will attempt to load the video twice, 404'ing each time, before giving up. This is what HTTP links still do.\n\nCurrent behavior: yt-dlp will see the 404 from the HTTPS link, and then VRC will immediately give up, not attempting to load the video in AVPro.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
