      "value": "@{62df7cd83e007e467295c4e1|full_name}: except that this wasn't the behavior before, and it's still not the behavior for http, only https, which leads me to believe this change may be unintentional.\n\nAgain, there are server configs where you may want to 404 yt-dlp/browser access, but allow AVPro. It's extremely niche, I know, but there's no reason to give up immediately after yt-dlp dies. Serving 404's is cheap, and it's only another 2 requests. Additionally, I wouldn't be surprised if other irrelevant yt-dlp errors also caused AVPro to not load otherwise valid content.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
