  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-05-05T05:29:28.285Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Prior to VRChat 1304, if an https video link errored out (e.g. 404'd), it would then be passed to AVPro directly to retry up to two times. Post-1304, VRC will give up immediately when an https link passed to yt-dlp errors out, and the link will not attempt to load in AVPro at that point.\n\nI'm aware this is an extremely minor and niche change, but I maintain a world that depended on the old retry behavior due to the https video server configuration. While I was able to work around this around by reconfiguring the server, I believe this may still be worth examining in the event that other yt-dlp error conditions don't correctly fall back to attempting AVPro direct-load.\n\nIt's also worth pointing out that http (not https) links will follow the previous behavior of two retries. Odd inconsistency for what I'd think should be the same code path.",
